ion is for  madu  can we use kingfisher duo for automation  of magmax microbiome kit  what are the pros and cons versus  kingfisher flex  we can use the duo for the magmax  microbiome kit it was  already tested and it gives you  this as the flex  so the source is uh basically  um we can use less control  because if if the customer has few  samples to process  they can go with the duo if they have  more than  12 samples to process they can use the  flex instrument processor to  use the 96 deep well plate and  also like the eels are similar as i  already mentioned  um the only cons for the duo is we  cannot process more than 12 samples at a  time  okay thank you so much madhu my next  question is for emily  what is the average time to process 96  samples using the high throughput  extraction high throughput pcr  open array workflow  so average time it does depend kind of  on what open array  plate you're doing but i would say the  average  time is about eight hours  and that's from start to finish that's  from you have your sample in hand to  have your results off the instrument  okay thanks emily my next question is  for madu this is our last question  for sars wastewater surveillance you  showed concentration of the water  samples using filters  what other concentration options do you  recommend  um there are like wide variety of  options and  included in the publications like  worldwide like some people do peg  precipitation  and some people do ultra centrifugation  but we didn't test all these  options with our magmax microbiome kit  but when time permits we wanted to test  the peg precipitation  on these wastewater samples um it seems  like it's gonna concentrate the  wastewater samples pretty well  because we have tested with the cell  culture media and it works pretty good  so we need to test more options on this  thank you again sasha madhu and emily  for your time today  and for your important research we would  also like to thank labruz and our  sponsors thermo fisher scientific  for underwriting today's educational  webcast  before we go i'd like to thank the  audience for joining us today  and for their interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted during the on-demand  period will be addressed by the speakers  via the contact information you provided  at the time of registration  this webcast can be viewed on demand lab  roots will alert you via email when it's  available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's live event  the next installment of the prep for  success webinar series takes place  february 11th and focuses on vaccine  development  so please join us for that until next  time  goodbye


